WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-VI

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.440
Hello.  Welcome back
to Lam Rim.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.580
Today we will review the
entire course.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.520
That's good for me.  I also want to review the material.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.680
By working through these individual modules

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.520
and then studying them at separate times,

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.880
you're essentially losing the flow of the entire lesson.

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:30.559
I was thinking it would be great today
if we could go back to the

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.560
beginning and go through the entire circuit of the

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.280
Lam Rim lecture that we had.

00:00:38.559 --> 00:00:42.799
I will implement that circuit based on the IDIMs,
on the concept images,

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.540
that we use to teach ACI teachers.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.220
ACI teachers

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.800
are expected to be able to look at
one of these images

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.480
and recognize the idea behind it.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:59.120
I think, Tim, we were talking about how many there would be?   A thousand or something like that?

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.800
How much?

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:08.639
500, or something like that.
Therefore, it's quite easy to conduct a test

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.493
to examine someone based solely on
pictures.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.160
Therefore, we are only
posting these pictures for you.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.800
So, I'm going to challenge you throughout this review session:

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.240
when we show you a picture,

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.000
I'll give you a second to see if you

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.533
can remember what the picture is about.

00:01:26.533 --> 00:01:28.000
Okay, and this is a pretty good review

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:32.479
of the entire course we're doing.
Okay, let's begin.  The

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.560
first picture, Sejii,

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.000
is meant to remind you

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.420
that we are in the midst of practices

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.360
for people of average ability,

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:52.440
and what they are trying to achieve is Nirvana.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:58.800
They are trying to escape the Wheel of Samsara, to
escape their own suffering.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.560
This is where the Buddha taught three practices

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:07.120
that will help you attain
your personal Nirvana.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:12.420
The third training is understanding emptiness,
understanding the pen.  The

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.880
second form of training is meditation.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:21.200
On a deeper level, both of these practices
can only be done in a quiet place,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:26.880
during specific times of the day, when you are truly focused on your meditation cushion.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.740
To a deeper level, both of these exercises
must be performed

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.865
at specific times of the day.

00:02:34.865 --> 00:02:39.540
But this training, the foundation of those two trainings, is treating others with kindness.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.280
You could call it morality.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.840
You could call it an ethical way of life,

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.800
but ultimately, it's about treating
other people kindly.

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:50.840
That's the foundation,

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.640
something that's always available to us throughout the day.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:57.900
This is one of the three extraordinary practices
of Buddhism,

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.659
serving as a means to help us attain Nirvana.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.049
And this is available to us throughout the day.

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:05.360
So in this picture,

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.360
you can see Sejii helping
Geshe Michael figure out his computer.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:14.640
That is one of the kindest things
young people can do for older people.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:20.959
Look at the next picture; can you remember
what it is?  Have

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.040
you guessed it yet?

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:34.080
This woman is paying her taxes.
What role does that make her within the Lam Rim system?

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.320
It made her...

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:41.360
a sorceress.  When I say a Shaman,
or a Tantric Master,

00:03:42.159 --> 00:03:44.544
I know the image you have
in your mind.

00:03:44.544 --> 00:03:48.140
That was some high-ranking Lama on a throne,
and they had a large yellow hat.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:57.760
Perhaps they're ringing a bell
and a little drum, and they...

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.751
And you think, "Oh, that's a sorcerer.
That's a real sorcerer."

00:04:00.751 --> 00:04:02.900
Or perhaps you're thinking of the old picture
of Nagarjuna,

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:06.739
and he, he was completely kind of mystical.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.959
In Lam Rim, what we learned

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:13.920
is that this woman

00:04:14.799 --> 00:04:17.439
has several children, she is married,

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:22.078
and she is a sorceress.
She is a true sorceress.

00:04:22.639 --> 00:04:27.459
Pabongka Rinpoche said, don't think that a Dharma Master has to sit on a throne and

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.660
recite certain Tantric rituals.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.960
What is this woman doing?

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.760
She is paying her taxes.  Being

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:42.840
honest with your tax money seems to be
really difficult in my country.  It

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:46.320
can take you weeks to
file your taxes

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:48.880
and to do them really carefully,

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.040
to do them completely honestly,

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.759
to pay every single penny that you owe.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.400
This led her...

00:04:56.479 --> 00:05:00.639
She received the first of the extraordinary trainings of a good person;  Be

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.880
kind to others.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.400
That makes her a true sorceress.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:09.920
Forget the pictures you have of Lamas
wearing large hats

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:11.700
and ringing bells.
Okay, that's easy.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.420
Anyone can do that.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:16.720
Being kind to others is difficult,

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:20.079
and maintaining your morals,
upholding your ethical standards, is

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.065
also difficult.  The

00:05:22.065 --> 00:05:24.700
next picture;

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:30.080
I'll give you a moment.
Do you remember what this is about?

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:39.240
The quote in Lam Rim is
TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA'I DGE SLONG 'OD DANG LDAN:

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.560
A person who is truly upholding
their vows,

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:46.720
truly upholding the principles of Buddhism,
especially the Ten Principles,

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.620
they shine, they truly shine.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:58.656
A person who is making a healthy, humble, simple effort to keep their commitments,

00:05:58.656 --> 00:06:01.360
to maintain good karma and be

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.000
kind to others,

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:07.519
they seem to have a certain peace
on their face;

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.160
they are radiating.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.260
When they walk into a room,
you know it.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:17.360
Everyone started to feel better, just
like Tim and Sejii.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:19.860
It is a light of the world.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.240
The Buddha said, those people are the light
of the world.

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:26.380
There is a Christian saying;

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:32.400
Don't put a candle under a basket; let the world see your happy faces.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:39.960
And that is a true guiding light
for the whole world.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:43.440
The next picture, IDIM #4.

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:57.600
This is a rock formation that I visited with my partner Veronica for her birthday during this Lam Rim course.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:06.940
They were talking about sunset,
which in Tibetan is called NUB PA.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:10.580
It is also a word for west
because the sun sets in the west;

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.500
NUB PA means

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:16.080
the sun is setting, and it's a very sad verb.

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:20.820
This is a very sad idea in Buddhism,

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:27.980
most famously found at the end of Abhidharma kosha, The Treasure House of Higher Wisdom.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:31.760
The Treasure
House of Higher Knowledge, written by
Vasubandhu, states:

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:39.060
"The sun of the Dharma, the light of the Dharma,
will set on this world."

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:43.440
We will lose the light of France in this world.  The world will descend into darkness.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:45.520
After a certain period of time,

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.560
the teachings of the Buddha will disappear
from this world.

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:56.060
First, they will fade from people's minds, but they will still remain in libraries.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:59.600
Those books are still in the libraries.  It is possible that these are libraries that John Brady has not yet found.

00:08:00.319 --> 00:08:04.239
And then they will disappear from the libraries,
and then they will vanish.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:11.840
I put this picture here because Papongka Rinpoche made a special point; he said,

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:19.520
"If you cannot keep your commitments, if you cannot maintain a kind attitude towards
others,

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:22.640
then we can say that the Dharma
has left this world."

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:26.319
The light of France has left this world
within you.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:30.780
The sun has set inside
your own chests, and

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:34.460
it would be very sad if we did not keep our vows.  The

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:36.560
next picture.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:48.200
We call this the "Love and
Compassion in the Time of the Virus" retreat.  The

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:55.440
main point is that during
that very difficult time in the world,

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.600
if you kept your commitments,

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.860
if you were kind to others

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.320
when things were scary and frightening
and the virus was spreading.

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.160
We don't know where,
we don't know how,

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:08.880
and we don't know how many
people will die.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:16.660
If, during those difficult times,
you do something kind for others,

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:19.160
it will be so much more powerful.

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:22.420
He mentioned, if you remember,
a 5-star Buddhist paradise.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.759
It's like a perfect place.

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:29.839
It's easy to be a good person;
everyone there is a good person.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:33.236
That's not a great achievement.
It's not a big deal,

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:35.220
and the seeds aren't that strong

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:38.580
to be kind in a group of kind people.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:42.880
Be kind when people are attacking you,
when everyone is afraid.

00:09:43.839 --> 00:09:47.518
When people aren't being kind to each other,
and to be someone who

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:54.060
stands up and shares things during
these difficult times –

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.340
that's an extremely pure person.

00:09:57.520 --> 00:10:01.500
That was a great achievement.  That's an
incredible karma, far more powerful.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:03.840
I think this virus is a very good time,

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:09.120
and it's a great opportunity for all of us
to prove

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:14.380
whether we are truly Buddhists.
And are we truly practicing the
Bodhisattva Path?

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:18.560
Can we help others
even when things are so difficult?  The

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.500
next picture.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:31.460
This picture is hard to remember;
I'm having trouble recalling it.

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:36.280
I'll give you a second
to try and figure out what this picture is about.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:43.840
Pabongka Rinpoche quoted from
several books.

00:10:44.959 --> 00:10:46.959
with an ending that is very, very common for
various books.

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:57.760
He quoted from a famous book,
BLO BZANG RGYAL BA'I BSTAN PA ... CIG,

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:02.720
praying that the teachings of
the Victorious

00:11:03.519 --> 00:11:05.519
Lobsang Drakpa, Je Tsongkapa, may

00:11:06.079 --> 00:11:08.079
spread throughout the world.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:12.720
You're probably thinking,
we've got access to the Internet.

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:16.000
We need to translate this Lam Rim
into many languages.

00:11:17.279 --> 00:11:21.679
We must strive to spread kindness
to as many people as possible.

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:31.200
That's the final part of the prayer, and we have to
step out of this Lam Rim class or video

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:35.860
and share the Dharma
with others.

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:38.280
We must spread France throughout the world.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:44.260
In this part of the Lam Rim,
Pabongka Rinpoche said:

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:50.660
the place where you must spread the Dharma is here,
in your own hearts.

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:56.160
Don't think that spreading the word means
trying to translate videos

00:11:56.160 --> 00:12:00.800
into more languages ​​or anything like
that.  That was a very important French influence.

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:05.240
But he said, if you spread it
in your own heart,

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:09.920
then of course it will spread outward because the world is coming from your heart,

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:11.519
really from your Heart Chakra.

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:16.860
The next picture is number 7.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:23.300
Try to remember what this picture is about.
I'll give you a second.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:31.680
This is one of my favorite topics;  to

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:42.000
have a personal relationship with another person,
just like these two people have.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:47.866
In my opinion, and in Tantra, it is one of the happiest things that can happen to you.

00:12:47.866 --> 00:12:51.860
It's one of the greatest things that
could happen to you guys.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:57.520
Anyone can tell you why the whole world is looking for a life partner,

00:12:58.399 --> 00:13:00.082
that it makes people happy.

00:13:00.082 --> 00:13:03.279
It's one of the greatest joys
when things go well.

00:13:04.399 --> 00:13:07.518
It's one of the greatest joys
you can have, but

00:13:08.399 --> 00:13:12.799
you know, and I know, when it doesn't go well,

00:13:13.519 --> 00:13:16.159
it's one of the greatest sorrows
in life.

00:13:16.959 --> 00:13:19.839
Why is that relevant to this course
right here?

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:29.120
If your morals are good,

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:31.360
that is the greatest happiness in
your life.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:37.040
And if you break your morals,
that's what will make you miserable.

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:40.320
It's like having a kind woman or man as your life partner, the

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:44.620
same person who can make you
completely happy, but

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:47.860
can also make you completely miserable.

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:52.400
So in this case, the Law,
your personal practice of kindness,

00:13:52.940 --> 00:13:56.240
good behavior, is being compared to
a life partner who

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:59.540
could or will create the best


00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.320
or the worst thing in your life—the
same person.

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:10.120
Next IDIM, number 8.

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:13.840
This is a complex image.
Let's see if you can remember!

00:14:15.519 --> 00:14:17.519
I'm going to have a drink of my green beverage.

00:14:18.639 --> 00:14:20.639
Thank you, Vimala.

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:33.560
This really represents a breach of
your commitments.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:39.720
Pulling out a weed represents breaking
your commitments.

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:45.260
Why would destroying this tree be considered a breach of
your commitment?

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:51.560
If you're a gardener,
you know that you should remove weeds

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:54.640
before the seeds are ready.

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:59.380
If you wait until the seeds
are ready to fall,

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.920
and then you pull out the weeds,

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:04.560
you will have sown about a thousand seeds.

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:11.260
In the next month or year, you will have thousands of weeds growing back.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:13.440
Therefore, you must attack
those weeds as soon as possible.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:19.140
This relates to a very radical statement

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:21.360
that the Buddha made:

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:27.900
DGE SLONG DAG SROG DANG BRAL ZHING
SHI BA NI BLA'I.  I would rather

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.240
die

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.479
than break your vows.
Why?

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:35.680
When you break your vows,

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.980
you are scattering seeds

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:42.660
that will continue to fall for many lifetimes.

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:49.740
If you die, you will destroy
a mind-body complex.

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:54.060
If you die, you will destroy
a very useful shrine,

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:57.360
a physical shrine and a mind.
You only lose one.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.560
But if you break your commitments,

00:16:01.279 --> 00:16:04.440
you will lose many complex mind-body relationships.

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:07.458
You have ruined your body and mind
over many lifetimes.

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:11.440
And just as you are scattering seeds

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:14.280
that will destroy many lives.

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:20.420
The Buddha said;  He would rather die than break
your vows, and

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:27.460
he was not speaking in parables.
He was speaking literally

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:31.280
when he said that.  I would rather die than break
my promises.

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:35.360
There's a joke in Lam Rim.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:44.320
We take a vow never to abandon
Bodhicitta, even if it means sacrificing
our lives.

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:52.480
There's a famous saying, "
All our lives we're waiting

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:54.720
to be thrown into prison

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:56.880
by some evil person."

00:16:57.199 --> 00:17:02.479
They come up to us, hold a knife to our throats, and say, “Give up
your Bodhisattva vows or die today.”

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.799
Then we say,

00:17:04.799 --> 00:17:06.480
“I choose to die.”

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:09.199
And they kill us.

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:13.280
I think we’ve all been waiting for this since
we took those vows.

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:18.300
We’ve all been waiting for these people to show up
with knives and threaten us.

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:22.960
But we are the ones holding the knives.
We threaten our Bodhisattva vows
every day.

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:31.840
We have to make this decision every day when we decide whether or not to keep our vows
carefully.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.860
It’s hard to find those people who
throw you in jail and say, “

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:41.440
I will kill you if you don’t give up
your Bodhisattva vows.”

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:46.720
The next picture.

